ping-attributable decline Q_recent / (A_aquifer * Sy_app) as a share of the observed decline averaged over the same aquifer area, applied to the irrigated-point decline (one basis for both). ft_per_af_ac is scaled the same way. sat_avail_ft[T] = years_p50[T] * decline_ft_yr, so X = 0 reproduces the county clock exactly; where the county clock is at the 100-year cap, sat_avail_ft[T] = max(100 * decline, sat_thick_p50 - T). Where median_below_threshold[T] is true the median acre is already below T and no gain can show at that T.","threshold_default_ft":30,"water_balance":{"method":"Water-balance link between reported pumping (WIMAS) and observed water-level change (wells).\n\nFollowing the approach of Butler et al. (2016, GRL), for each area the annual change in mean winter water level\ndWL_t (Jan t minus Jan t-1, ft) is regressed on the reported groundwater pumping of the intervening irrigation season\nQ_{t-1} expressed as a depth over the area's aquifer footprint (ft = AF / acres):\n\n    dWL_t = a + beta * Q_{t-1}/A + e_t          (physically beta = -1/Sy_app, a = net inflow / Sy_app)\n\nSy_app is an \"apparent specific yield\" on a gross-pumping basis (it absorbs irrigation return flow and lateral flow).\nCounty slopes are combined with a physical prior beta ~ -1/Sy, Sy in 0.10-0.20 (PRIORS['sy']) by precision weighting\non 1/Sy, then partially pooled toward the GMD mean (empirical Bayes). The pumping-attributable decline used by the\nscenarios is   decline_from_pumping = -beta_post * Q_recent / A   and the response coefficient per irrigated acre is\nft_per_af_ac = -beta_post * irrigated_acres / A  (ft of decline per AF/acre applied on the county's irrigated acres).","summary":{"fe_within":{"beta":-7.2209,"se":0.5918,"r2":0.1379,"n":933,"sy_app":0.1385},"cross_section":{"beta":-4.7443,"se":0.3166,"jackknife_se":0.3831,"r2":0.9034,"n":26,"intercept":0.0348,"sy_app":0.2108,"years":[1991,2026]},"posterior":{"inv_sy":4.9034,"inv_sy_se":0.3669,"sy_app":0.2039,"sy_app_8